# === CREDENTIALS — never commit these ===
# A service-account JSON bypasses all security rules. It is root access to the
# database, not "an admin login". If one of these ever gets committed, revoke the
# key in the Google Cloud console immediately — deleting the commit is not enough.
*serviceAccount*.json
*service-account*.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Firebase local state
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
ui-debug.log
database-debug.log
pubsub-debug.log

# Emulator seed data — regenerate from backups instead of committing
emulator-data/

# Node
node_modules/
package-lock.json
npm-debug.log*

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
